---
description: How CREW app state is structured — where mutations and selectors go
alwaysApply: true
---

CREW state is ONE `AppData` signal, persisted as one blob, split across a kernel +
feature stores. Do NOT reintroduce a single god service or a second source of truth.

- `AppStateStore` (`src/app/services/app-state.store.ts`) — kernel: owns the
  `data = signal<AppData>()`, `init()`, `persist(notify)`, `finishFormSession()`.
- Feature stores own one domain's MUTATIONS each, sharing state via
  `private readonly data = this.state.data;` then `this.data.update(...)` +
  `void this.state.persist(notify)`:
  `reference-lists.store`, `crew.store`, `passenger.store`, `dg-manifest.store`,
  `reefer.store`, `document-settings.store`, `forms.store`.
- `StorageService` — thin facade holding ALL read SELECTORS (`computed`), plus
  ship/voyage core, snapshots, import/export. Delegates persistence to the kernel.
- `app-data-normalizer.ts` — pure normalization/migration (no signals, no IO).
  Schema is additive: read every field as `raw.X ?? default`; no destructive migrations.

RULE when adding state logic:
- New write → add a method to the matching FEATURE STORE (not StorageService).
- New read → add a `computed` SELECTOR to StorageService.
- A component injects `storage` for reads and the relevant store for writes.

See `CLAUDE.md` ("State management architecture") for the full description.
